---
title: Pressure Cooker Chicken and Rice
servings: 4
course: dinner
image: https://img.youtube.com/vi/lbhBWI-r1IY/maxresdefault.jpg
tags: pressure-cooker, chicken, rice, one-pan
source: https://youtu.be/lbhBWI-r1IY
time: 20m
---

Heat a #pressure cooker{} on high.

In a #bowl{}, season @chicken thigh{600%g} with @olive oil{1%tbsp}, @smoked paprika{1%tbsp}, @ground cumin{1%tbsp}, @ground coriander{1%tsp}, and @salt{1%tsp}. Mix well to coat.

Add @olive oil{1%tbsp} to the pressure cooker. Seal off the chicken until browned, then pull it out and set aside.

Add @onion{1%chopped}, @red chilli{2%chopped}, and @garlic{0.5%head}(chopped) to the pot. Sweat that down for ~{1%minute}.

Add @long grain rice{400%g}(washed) and stir through.

Pour in @chicken stock{680%ml} and bring it to a simmer.

Add @green beans{150%g}(cut) and stir them through.

Place the chicken back on top along with any resting liquid.

Put the lid on and bring to high pressure. Once it starts whistling, cook for ~{6%minutes}.

Release the pressure, remove the lid, and transfer the chicken out to a plate.

Give the rice a stir to fluff it up a bit.

Plate up the rice, arrange the chicken on top, and garnish with lots of chopped @fresh parsley{}.
